    /// `board/hinge` — renders 22 on a 26×24 viewBox, 1.9pt effective stroke, --color-ink.
    ///
    /// Exception 2 of the board's three, and the only non-square product glyph. Its six
    /// interior dots are filled at r=1 rather than stroked, which is why it holds up when the
    /// board peek shrinks it. renderSize is the width — the height follows the 26×24 aspect,
    /// because the board's rule is that a non-square mark centred in a square slot is correct
    /// and a stretched one is not.
    static let boardHinge = IconGlyph(
        name: "board/hinge",
        viewBox: CGSize(width: 26, height: 24),
        renderSize: 22,
        productRenderSizes: [22],
        // Exception to the 2.0 rule, kept deliberately. The rule would push its attribute to
        // 2.4, a 26% jump. The heavier frame closes in on the six r=1 interior dots and the
        // mark reads as a blob at true size. It is also the one glyph that never appears beside
        // another, so matching the rail's weight buys nothing.
        strokeWidth: 1.9,
        colorToken: "--color-ink",
        elements: [
            IconElement(
